/* Modern theme for the generic confirm dialog. #panel's own background/border/box-shadow recipe
   (matching sys_menu.rcss's #panel -- both are small forged-iron dialogs with no hero-banner), the
   shell-edge/groove, and the well's recessed fill all moved to generic_confirm_dialog_bg.rcss --
   see that file's own comment for why (item3D layering). This file is layout/content only now,
   except for `.gcd-header-rail` below -- an in-flow, CSS-painted title banner using Login/SysMenu's
   own header-rail/hero-banner recipes and hardware at their own full size, unlike those two which
   paint their header chrome as part of the shared forged-dialog shell. */

/* #panel is centered via .center-both, not a GetProperty()-read-back calc -- same reasoning as
   remember_password_prompt.rcss. dp throughout: this is a LayoutMode::Dialog window (no
   transform:scale(root_scale)), not one of the root_scale-tracking inventory-family windows.
   Deliberately no paint here -- generic_confirm_dialog_bg.rcss's own #panel carries the same
   width/height so the two documents' panels align exactly; see that file's comment. */
/* height grew from the original 160dp by +18dp (matching .gcd-header-rail's own growth from 20dp
   to the full 38dp -- see that rule's own comment) so the header could take its accurate, unscaled
   size without shrinking the content area below what it had before that rail existed -- .gcd-body's
   own top/bottom stay the same 10dp/54dp, so this height increase becomes exactly the content
   area's own gain (bg document's #panel must match this exactly, see that file's own comment). */
#panel {
	width: 230dp;
	height: 178dp;
	font-family: "token(font-body)";
	font-size: 12dp;
	color: token(text-primary);
}

/* Message well -- layout only now (position/overflow/flex); the recessed fill that used to come
   from base.rcss's .modern-content-well lives in generic_confirm_dialog_bg.rcss's
   .gcd-bg-content-fill instead (same left/right/top/bottom, so the fill still lines up exactly
   behind this box). Text sits directly on it, scrolling (overflow: hidden auto) rather than
   growing the panel -- see the top-level generic_confirm_dialog.rml's own comment for why (the
   Quest window's .quest-contents proves the same technique).

   top+bottom (not top+height) deliberately -- this element also has flex centering below, and this
   engine's box model is content-box only (no box-sizing support anywhere in this codebase); an
   explicit height combined with flex/padding on children pushed the box past its intended bottom
   edge and visually overlapped the button row. Anchoring both edges keeps the box's outer size
   exactly (right - left) x (bottom - top) regardless of its content's own layout. */
/* .gcd-content-row is this box's only flex child -- the optional header banner
   (.gcd-header-rail, hidden when untitled) is position:absolute, NOT stacked above it in the same
   flex column (an earlier design had both as flex siblings; centering them as a single group put
   text visibly too far down whenever the header was shorter than the box, and a later flex-start
   attempt fixed that but lost centering entirely -- see .gcd-body.has-title's own comment below).
   justify-content/align-items center content-row within whatever space is actually available,
   which the has-title padding-top override (below) narrows to just the space below the header.

   padding is deliberately minimal, NOT a direct copy of the reference's own
   `.confirm-dialog .window__body{padding:20px 18px}` figure -- this box's own pre-existing
   left/right:16dp ALREADY plays the outer-inset role the reference's own
   `.window__body{margin:6px 8px 8px}` plays (same job, same edge), and at 16/230=~7% of this
   panel's fixed width is already close to (in fact more generous than) the reference's own
   combined margin+padding ratio once you account for the reference's window being free to grow
   and absorb a bigger number where this panel's own height is fixed. Two earlier attempts both
   overshot by treating the reference's raw padding figure as an ADDITION on top of that existing
   16dp inset instead of the small remainder needed to reach a comparable total -- first `6dp
   18dp` (combined ~15% per side), then `2dp 3dp` (still visibly too much extra inset in-game).
   This is intentionally closer to zero: just enough that text doesn't touch the well's own inner
   edge, not a second independent margin.

   Safe to add directly to THIS box specifically because it's sized via left/right/top/bottom
   (anchored edges), not an explicit width/height -- padding only shrinks the content area those
   edges enclose, it can't push the box's own outer size past them the way it would on a
   `width:100%`/`height:100%` child (this engine has no box-sizing support, see the comment above).
   Both .gcd-header-rail and .gcd-content-row inherit the inset via their own width:100%, so this
   insets the whole column, not just the text -- .gcd-header-rail itself stays without its own
   margin/padding (reference's `.window__header{margin:7px 8px 0;padding:0 11px}`) since it's that
   same width:100% child, so adding either there directly would hit the exact hazard just
   described; it already picks up an equivalent inset for free from this padding instead. */
.gcd-body {
	position: absolute;
	left: 16dp;
	right: 16dp;
	top: 10dp;
	bottom: 54dp;
	padding: 1dp;
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: column;
	justify-content: center;
	align-items: center;
}
/* With a title, .gcd-header-rail moves out of the flex flow entirely (position:absolute below) and
   this reserves its space as padding-top instead (38dp height + 4dp gap) -- content-row is then
   .gcd-body's ONLY flex participant again, so its own `justify-content:center` centers content
   within the space actually left after the header, not a [header,content] group centered as a
   unit within the WHOLE box (that earlier approach put the group's midpoint below the true midpoint
   of the remaining space, since the header's own height counted toward the thing being centered --
   visibly "too far down"/"not centered" in-game -- and a later flex-start attempt fixed the gap but
   lost centering entirely, hugging content to the top instead). Taking the header out of the flex
   flow sidesteps needing `.gcd-content-row`'s own flex-grow to reliably claim exactly 100% of
   whatever space is left, since there's only one flex child again either way. */
.gcd-body.has-title {
	padding-top: 42dp;
}
/* Optional title banner -- uses base.rcss's own .modern-header-rail paint recipe (copied rather
   than shared since the exact position differs) at its own full, unscaled 38dp height (matching
   .modern-header-rail's own 38dp exactly -- see the rivet/accent/stud rules below for why scaling
   it down first was wrong). position:absolute (not a flex child of .gcd-body) so it doesn't
   compete with .gcd-content-row for space in .gcd-body's own centering -- see that rule's own
   comment. severity_warning/_error recolor it (warning: amber-recolored rail; error: recolored
   toward .modern-title-plate's own crimson hero-banner palette) -- no behavior is gated on them,
   only styling (see the .rml's own comment). */
.gcd-header-rail {
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	right: 0;
	top: 0;
	display: flex;
	align-items: center;
	justify-content: center;
	height: 38dp;
	background-color: token(metal-dark);
	decorator:
		linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(205, 184, 129, 13), transparent 31%),
		linear-gradient(to bottom, token(metal-rail), #171813 45%, token(metal-rail-dark));
	border-width: 1dp;
	border-color: token(border-rail);
	border-bottom-color: #171812;
	box-shadow:
		inset 0 1dp 0 rgba(235, 218, 169, 18),
		inset 0 -1dp 0 #000000,
		0 2dp 4dp rgba(0, 0, 0, 133);
}
/* Same display/.hidden cascade-tie fix as every other data-class-hidden toggle in this file --
   .gcd-header-rail sets its own `display`, so an earlier same-specificity `.hidden { display:
   none; }` (base.rcss) loses the tie without this later, more specific override. */
.gcd-header-rail.hidden { display: none; }
/* Center rivet -- .modern-joint's (base.rcss) own exact values, not a scaled-down guess (an
   earlier 10x10dp/top:-6dp scale-down was flagged as "not accurately positioned" in-game; using
   the same proven recipe verbatim, on a rail now tall enough to fit it, is the fix). Plain/warning
   look only -- hidden for severity_error, which uses the twin side studs below instead (see the
   .rml's own comment). */
.gcd-header-joint {
	position: absolute;
	left: 50%;
	top: -8dp;
	width: 13dp;
	height: 13dp;
	margin-left: -6.5dp;
	pointer-events: none;
	background-color: token(metal-groove);
	border-width: 1dp;
	border-color: #484638;
	transform: rotate(45deg);
	box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2dp #0c0d0b;
}
/* .modern-header-accent's (base.rcss) own exact values -- same reasoning as the joint above. */
.gcd-header-accent {
	position: absolute;
	left: 7dp;
	right: 7dp;
	bottom: 2dp;
	height: 1dp;
	pointer-events: none;
	opacity: 0.35;
	decorator: linear-gradient(to right,
		transparent,
		token(metal-warm-edge) 30%,
		#84754e 50%,
		token(metal-warm-edge) 70%,
		transparent);
}
/* Twin diamond studs -- .login-hero-cap/-left/-right's (login.rcss) own exact values, same
   reasoning as the joint above. severity_error only, replacing the joint+accent above (see the
   .rml's own comment). */
.gcd-header-cap {
	position: absolute;
	top: 50%;
	width: 11dp;
	height: 11dp;
	margin-top: -5.5dp;
	background-color: #24100a;
	border-width: 1dp;
	border-color: #6a2a19;
	transform: rotate(45deg);
	pointer-events: none;
	box-shadow:
		inset 1dp 1dp 0 rgba(255, 208, 145, 9),
		inset -1dp -1dp 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 173);
}
.gcd-header-cap-left { left: 8dp; }
.gcd-header-cap-right { right: 8dp; }
/* font-size now matches .modern-header-title's (base.rcss) own 13dp exactly -- was scaled to 11dp
   for the shorter first-attempt rail, no longer needed now that the rail is full-size. */
.gcd-header-title {
	color: token(text-warm);
	font-family: "token(font-title)";
	font-size: 13dp;
	font-weight: 500;
	letter-spacing: 0.2dp;
	font-effect: shadow(0dp 1dp #000000);
}
.gcd-header-rail.warning {
	border-color: token(semantic-warning);
	box-shadow:
		inset 0 1dp 0 rgba(255, 208, 130, 30),
		inset 0 -1dp 0 #000000,
		0 2dp 4dp rgba(0, 0, 0, 133);
}
.gcd-header-rail.warning .gcd-header-title { color: token(semantic-warning); }
.gcd-header-rail.error {
	background-color: token(metal-title-face);
	decorator:
		linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(255, 217, 158, 18), transparent 34%),
		linear-gradient(to bottom, #55150f 0%, token(metal-title-face) 56%, token(metal-title-face-dark) 100%);
	border-color: token(border-title);
	box-shadow:
		inset 0 1dp 0 rgba(255, 208, 145, 23),
		inset 0 -1dp 0 #080201,
		0 2dp 5dp rgba(0, 0, 0, 140);
}
/* Distinct brighter gold vs the plain rail's own token(text-warm)/#d6ad45 title -- matches the
   reference's own .hero-banner__title, a color used only for this hero-banner look, not shared
   with the plain header. No existing token matches it exactly, so hardcoded, same as this block's
   other hero-banner-specific colors above. */
.gcd-header-rail.error .gcd-header-title { color: #e1b94e; }

/* Row holding the item3D anchor + text column -- was .gcd-body's own direct row layout until the
   header banner above needed to sit outside it (see that rule's own comment). width:100% so it
   spans .gcd-body's full inset width same as before (the row used to BE .gcd-body, which already
   had that width implicitly); flex:1 1 auto claims whatever height the (possibly-hidden) banner
   above doesn't. */
.gcd-content-row {
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: row;
	justify-content: center;
	align-items: center;
	width: 100%;
	flex: 1 1 auto;
}
/* Holds lines/input-row/progress-track -- everything .gcd-content-row used to flex-center
   directly before #gcd_item3d_anchor needed to sit beside it instead of above/below it (see that
   element's own comment below and the .rml's). Fills .gcd-content-row's full height explicitly
   (rather than relying on align-items, which wouldn't stretch under align-items:center) so its
   own overflow:auto has a real bound to scroll within once content (mainly `lines`) grows taller
   than the panel -- see the scrollbar rules below.

   overflow is `overflow-x, overflow-y` (CSS shorthand order) -- `hidden auto`, NOT `auto hidden`,
   is deliberate: horizontal never needs to scroll (`.gcd-line` wraps within a fixed width), and
   this engine only ever instantiates a scrollbarvertical element when overflow-y is Auto/Scroll,
   never Hidden (confirmed against RmlUi/Source/Core/Layout/ContainerBox.cpp) -- getting this
   order backwards silently means no scrollbar is ever created, regardless of text length.

   pointer-events: auto is required here too -- base.rcss's `body { pointer-events: none; }`
   inherits down to every descendant that doesn't explicitly opt back in (same reason `.btn`/
   `.checkbox-row` each set their own `pointer-events: auto`), and the scrollbar's generated
   slidertrack/sliderbar are real DOM children of THIS element, so they inherit whatever this
   element's own computed value is -- without this, the whole scrollbar (track clicks, thumb drag)
   silently can't receive any mouse events at all. */
.gcd-text-col {
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: column;
	justify-content: center;
	align-items: center;
	height: 100%;
	flex: 1 1 auto;
	overflow: hidden auto;
	pointer-events: auto;
}
/* Minimal flat-color scrollbar (no decorator images, matching this file's own progress-bar/keypad
   styling) -- .gcd-text-col is the first scrollable element in this theme, so there's no existing
   scrollbar styling to reuse; RmlUi generates real child elements for these (scrollbarvertical/
   slidertrack/sliderbar), not pseudo-elements. Arrow buttons collapsed to 0 size -- drag-only,
   simplest usable affordance for a narrow well. */
.gcd-text-col scrollbarvertical {
	width: 6dp;
	margin: 0;
}
.gcd-text-col scrollbarvertical slidertrack {
	background-color: token(metal-rail-dark);
}
/* Steel gray, matching .gcd-header-rail's own metal-rail palette rather than the gold accent used
   elsewhere in this dialog (progress-bar fill, etc.) -- ties the scrollbar to the header hardware. */
.gcd-text-col scrollbarvertical sliderbar {
	background-color: token(metal-edge);
}
.gcd-text-col scrollbarvertical sliderbar:hover,
.gcd-text-col scrollbarvertical sliderbar:active {
	background-color: token(metal-highlight);
}
.gcd-text-col scrollbarvertical sliderarrowdec,
.gcd-text-col scrollbarvertical sliderarrowinc {
	width: 0;
	height: 0;
}
.gcd-text-col scrollbarhorizontal {
	height: 0;
}
/* font-size/line-height explicit and smaller than #panel's own 12dp default -- reference's
   .confirm-dialog__message is deliberately subtler/smaller than the header title (10px vs 13px),
   this previously just inherited the panel default instead. */
.gcd-line {
	display: block;
	width: 100%;
	text-align: center;
	white-space: normal;
	color: token(text-secondary);
	font-size: 10dp;
	line-height: 15dp;
	font-effect: shadow(0dp 1dp #000000);
}
.gcd-line.bold { font-weight: bold; color: token(text-warm); }

/* Invisible position reference for the native 3D item-preview render pass
   (GenericConfirmDialog.cpp's Render3D()); fixed reference-space size matching
   C3DItemCommonMsgBox's own MSGBOX_3DITEM_WIDTH/HEIGHT (40x40, CommonMessageBox.h). Renders
   nothing itself.

   position: static overrides base.rcss's `.layout-anchor { position: absolute; ... }` -- that
   class assumes its own explicit top/left elsewhere (main_frame.rcss's #item_hotkey_anchor, a
   fixed legacy coordinate), which this anchor doesn't have: it's meant to flow as an ordinary
   flex child of .gcd-body itself (a row, sibling of .gcd-text-col), not be pulled out of it. */
.gcd-item3d-anchor {
	position: static;
	width: 40dp;
	height: 40dp;
	flex-shrink: 0;
	margin-right: 8dp;
}
/* Same display/.hidden cascade-tie fix as .gcd-header-rail above -- this anchor is now conditionally
   hidden (data-class-hidden="!has_item3d") so .gcd-text-col alone fills the row when there's no
   item3D, instead of always reserving a 40dp-wide empty slot. */
.gcd-item3d-anchor.hidden { display: none; }

/* Optional text-entry field -- see the .rml's own comment for the NumericKeypad-vs-Text split.
   `.btn.gcd-keypad-btn`/`.gcd-keypad-delete` override `.btn`'s own `position: absolute` back to
   static so they can flex-wrap into a grid instead of stacking on top of each other. */
.gcd-input-row {
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: column;
	align-items: center;
	margin-top: 4dp;
}
/* Same display/.hidden cascade-tie fix as .gcd-header-rail above -- without this, `data-class-hidden`
   toggling "hidden" on this row has no visible effect since `display: flex` above always wins the
   tie against base.rcss's earlier-declared `.hidden { display: none; }`. */
.gcd-input-row.hidden { display: none; }
.gcd-keypad-display {
	color: token(text-warm);
	font-weight: bold;
	letter-spacing: 4dp;
	min-height: 14dp;
	margin-bottom: 4dp;
}
.gcd-keypad-grid {
	display: flex;
	flex-wrap: wrap;
	justify-content: center;
	width: 150dp;
}
.gcd-keypad-grid.hidden { display: none; } /* same cascade-tie fix as .gcd-input-row above */
.btn.gcd-keypad-btn, .btn.gcd-keypad-delete {
	position: static;
	width: 26dp;
	height: 18dp;
	margin: 1dp;
	font-size: 9dp;
}
/* Position reference only, same idea as .gcd-item3d-anchor -- the native g_pSingleTextInputBox
   widget draws on top of this natively, nothing renders through RmlUi here for Mode::Text.
   position: static for the same reason .gcd-item3d-anchor needs it -- see that rule's comment. */
.gcd-input-anchor {
	position: static;
	width: 150dp;
	height: 18dp;
}

/* Optional progress bar (CProgressMsgBox/CCursedTempleProgressMsgBox) -- same
   `x_fraction * 100 + '%'` fill technique main_frame.rml's own HP/MP/AG/SD/EXP gauges prove. */
.gcd-progress-track {
	width: 150dp;
	height: 10dp;
	margin-top: 4dp;
	background-color: token(surface-recessed);
	border: 1dp token(border-inner);
	border-radius: token(radius-sm)dp;
}
.gcd-progress-fill {
	height: 100%;
	background-color: token(accent-gold);
}

/* Divider between the message well and the button row -- base.rcss's .modern-footer, repositioned
   to sit just above the buttons instead of flush with the panel's bottom edge. top values below
   (here and on the buttons) are +18dp over their original figures, matching #panel's own +18dp
   height growth -- both are `top`-anchored (not `bottom`), so without this shift they'd have
   stayed put while the panel's bottom edge moved 18dp further away, opening a gap. */
.gcd-footer {
	left: 8dp;
	right: 8dp;
	top: 132dp;
	bottom: auto;
}

.btn.gcd-btn-primary, .btn.gcd-btn-secondary {
	top: 138dp;
	width: 60dp;
	height: 25dp;
	line-height: 25dp;
}
.gcd-btn-primary   { left: 32dp; }
.gcd-btn-primary.solo { left: 85dp; }
.gcd-btn-secondary { left: 138dp; }
